{"name":"Seagull Beach","hex":"#c9bbb4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seagull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several white, often dark-backed birds of the family Laridae having long, pointed wings and short legs.","The symbol ̼, which combines under a letter as a sort of accent."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run in the back line rather than concentrate on primary positional duties in open play.","To use a British Seagull outboard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seagull"},{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gull","blocks":[{"text":"Gulls, informally called seagulls, are seabirds of the subfamily Larinae. They are most closely related to terns and skimmers, and are placed with them in the family Laridae. They are also related, more distantly, to auks and skuas, and more distantly still to waders. Until the 21st century, most gulls were placed in the genus Larus, but that arrangement is now considered polyphyletic, leading to the readoption and revision of several genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG/330px-Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gull"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/1280px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Immature (probably 2nd year) Armenian gull in flight, flying over Lake Sevan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArmenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg/500px-Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg/500px-Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Pacific gull is a large white-headed gull with a distinctively heavy bill.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th